Third-party components
======================

This project calls libass through cgo. Binary redistributors must include
the applicable license notices for every native library shipped in a package.
The packaging scripts collect installed notices; the resulting archive must
be audited before public redistribution. No subtitle font files are bundled.
The optional Fyne GUI embeds toolkit UI fonts, with their upstream notices
collected under licenses/go-modules along with its transitive Go dependencies.

Application icon:

* Google Material Icons, "subtitles": Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/google/material-design-icons
  Original: src/av/subtitles/materialicons/24px.svg
  Modified with a white glyph, blue/teal background and application-icon layout.
  Full license: licenses/material-icons/LICENSE in desktop packages.
  Source license: internal/desktop/assets/LICENSE-material-icons.

Direct Go dependencies (versions are recorded in go.mod and go.sum):

* github.com/go-text/typesetting: Unlicense OR BSD-3-Clause; font metadata scanning
  https://github.com/go-text/typesetting/blob/v0.3.5/LICENSE
* fyne.io/fyne/v2: BSD-3-Clause; bundled UI fonts and graphics sources have
  their own notices, collected recursively from the runtime dependency graph
  https://github.com/fyne-io/fyne/blob/master/LICENSE
* github.com/spf13/pflag: BSD-3-Clause
  https://github.com/spf13/pflag/blob/master/LICENSE
* github.com/ncruces/zenity: MIT; Windows native file dialogs only
  https://github.com/ncruces/zenity/blob/v0.10.14/LICENSE
* golang.org/x/text: BSD-3-Clause; some data files have additional notices
  https://go.googlesource.com/text/+/refs/heads/master/LICENSE

Native renderer and common transitive components:

* libass: ISC
  https://github.com/libass/libass/blob/master/COPYING
* FreeType: FreeType License or GPL-2.0; use the FreeType License option
  https://freetype.org/license.html
  Portions of this software are copyright (c) The FreeType Project
  (https://freetype.org/). All rights reserved.
* HarfBuzz: MIT-style; see its complete COPYING file
  https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz/blob/main/COPYING
* FriBidi: LGPL-2.1-or-later
  https://github.com/fribidi/fribidi/blob/master/COPYING

The exact native dependency graph depends on the platform and installed
packages. Build information is included in generated packages. Windows and
macOS builds statically link third-party native libraries into the executable.
Only operating-system libraries/frameworks remain dynamically linked.
No subtitle font files are bundled. The private macOS Graphite2 build uses the MIT
license option; its version and source checksum are recorded in the package.

Static development packages are NOT complete redistribution-compliance
bundles. LGPL components can include FriBidi and, through HarfBuzz, GLib.
Before redistribution, audit every linked component and provide the applicable
corresponding sources, notices, and object files or other relinking materials
and instructions needed to relink with modified LGPL libraries. Preserve
users' applicable modification/reverse-engineering rights. The build scripts
collect notices but do not automatically prepare these source/relinking
materials. This requirement is not removed by shipping only one executable.

FFmpeg is used only for development tests and is not bundled by this project.
Its own license depends on its build configuration.
